# Asking the user

`AskUserQuestion` is a Claude Code tool; it does not exist in Cursor. When a skill or rule says
`AskUserQuestion`, use this ladder instead:

1. `AskQuestion` (native) if it is in your tool catalog.
2. Otherwise (`Tool not found` — Auto, Grok, Cloud), the MCP tool `ask_questions` from the
   `cursor-ask` server: 1-4 `questions`, each with `id`, `prompt`, 2-6 `options` `{ id, label }`,
   optional `recommendedId`. It blocks until the user answers.
3. If neither is available or elicitation fails, ask in 1-2 short sentences of prose.

Never use a `*-decisions` canvas or long A/B/C lists in prose as a substitute. Never assume the
recommended option without an answer.
